    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Two young women on oral contraceptives for 4 and 6 years respectively died of severe myocardial infarction and shock. Autopsy discovered in both patients multiple thromboses in the coronary, intracardiac, and in the collateral aortic circulation. Since smoking, hyperlipidemia, hypertension and coronary atherosclerosis were not risk factors, oral contraception seems to have been the only cause for both thrombotic accidents."
    }
